  "verbalization": "Dl-Isoindolmycin appears to have a shared target of SNU-387, which is implicated in the target of multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and Dendocarbin K. All three compounds are linked to HepG2, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving SNU-387. The evidence suggests that Dl-Isoindolmycin may act through a common pathway, possibly by targeting SNU-387, which in turn affects HepG2. The presence of multiple targets for SNU-387 and their subsequent effect on HepG2 implies that the drug may exert its influence through a shared molecular mechanism, potentially involving the modulation of a specific biological process or pathway. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Dl-Isoindolmycin interacts with HepG2 via a mechanism involving SNU-387, which is a key intermediate in the target network.",
